        {
          "metadata": {
            "label": "Smpp Caller",
            "description": "Submits messages (`submit_sm`) on the same SMSC session the `Listener` receives on.\n\nObtained by declaring it as a parameter of a remote method — never constructed:\n\n```ballerina\nremote function onDeliverSm(smpp:Sms sms, smpp:Caller caller) returns error? {\n    smpp:SubmitResult r = check caller->submit({\n        destinationAddress: sms.sourceAddress,\n        shortMessage: \"reply text\"\n    });\n}\n```\n\nDeclaring the parameter is opt-in: a service that only declares `smpp:Sms` keeps\nworking unchanged. The parameter is matched by TYPE, not position — `(Sms, Caller)` and\n`(Caller, Sms)` are both accepted (unlike `mqtt`, which enforces caller-last; like\n`ftp`, which binds by type — and stricter than both: an optional-typed `smpp:Caller?`\nparameter or a rest parameter is rejected at attach, not silently left `()`).\n\nOne `Caller` exists per listener and stays valid across rebinds: every submit\nresolves the listener's *current* session, so a `Caller` captured before a drop\nsubmits on the fresh session after the rebind. Requires `bindType: TRANSCEIVER` — a\n`RECEIVER` bind cannot transmit, and `submit` on one fails fast with a clear error\nnaming the fix.\n\nNot `distinct`, matching the other stdlib Callers, so a future `smpp:Client` can\nsatisfy the same shape.",
            "icon": "https://bcentral-packageicons.azureedge.net/images/ballerina_smpp_1.0.0.png",
            "data": {
              "isAgentSupport": false
            }
          },
          "codedata": {
            "node": "NEW_CONNECTION",
            "org": "ballerina",
            "module": "smpp",
            "packageName": "smpp",
            "object": "Caller",
            "symbol": "init",
            "version": "1.0.0",
            "isGenerated": false
          },
          "enabled": true
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "label": "Blob Caller",
            "description": "The context object passed to a listener service's handlers, bound to the event's container\nand exposing a subset of `Client` to act on the event's blob. It cannot be instantiated by\nuser code.",
            "icon": "https://bcentral-packageicons.azureedge.net/images/ballerinax_azure.storage.blob_1.0.1.png",
            "data": {
              "isAgentSupport": false
            }
          },
          "codedata": {
            "node": "NEW_CONNECTION",
            "org": "ballerinax",
